{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
  "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Kentucky",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue before you today, of whether or not police can impermissibly create exigent circumstances, arises from the improper suppression of reasonably seized evidence after a reasonable warrantless entry. The test set forth by the Kentucky Supreme Court is improper for several reasons, the first of which is that this Court has routinely held that the subjective intent of police officers when effecting a warrantless entry is irrelevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where did the Kentucky Supreme Court say that it was looking to a subjective state of mind on the part of the police?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kentucky",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The test that the Commonwealth would propose is a simple lawfulness test. Now, under this test, as long as an officer behaves lawfully, there should be no suppression of evidence seized after an otherwise reasonable search."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Farley",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The smell of marijuana would give probable cause to obtain a search warrant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Respondent's brief in opposition, he argued that there was insufficient evidence of exigency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. O'CONNELL: Yes, I think that under this Court -- the way that this Court has interpreted Fourth Amendment warrant exceptions, as long as there is no violation of the Fourth Amendment, that is okay. The police officers can rely on any ensuing exigency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What are the objections to adding in the alternative \"or in bad faith\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, I -- I think the Court is interested in taking the case on the question whether or not the police may create exigent circumstances and use those exigent circumstances to enter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is because that behavior is reasonable, it is not made unreasonable by the fact that evidence may be destroyed, and so suppression would not be the remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. So you agree that -- that the court below is wrong because what they say, as I read it, is irrespective of how reasonably the police behave, if it is reasonably foreseeable that their tactic will create exigent circumstances -- and I would think it's reasonably foreseeable, when you knock on the door very politely and say \"The police,\" that somebody might shout out \"Hide the pot\"; all right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The appropriate test is the test that we propose. Under our test, the police act unreasonably when they convey the impression to an -- to a reasonable person that entry is imminent and inevitable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And to the extent that \"lawful\" is defined as a synonym for \"unreasonable\" and to the extent that there does not need to be a completed antecedent Fourth Amendment violation, we would agree."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what does that have to do with the -- the police officers' lawfulness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would like this Court to adopt the test that we have proposed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Which is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e864eca0a453-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have any doubt that it's unlawful for a police officer to threaten to burst into a home?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1272",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "e864eca0a453a831959d2f72710e99833e27d1b0c2f47543510b1a5fb7615fd4",
